Visually, it looks very similar to the Mark VII and Mark VIII with its classic red-and-gold paint scheme, but Tony redesigned the legs, hips, and lower abdominal plating to give the armor a less bulky, more streamlined silhouette. In Iron Man 3, the Mark IX flies in during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig and briefly steps in to protect Pepper Potts. During the battle, Pepper is knocked into a container stack by an Extremis soldier, and when Tony lands to assist her, the suit's leg is sliced off by an Extremis-enhanced enemy before Pepper herself later destroys the suit using one of its repulsor gauntlets to kill Aldrich Killian.
